WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
The results are strong on both fronts.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.680
On QM9, the scaled spherical CNN reaches state of the art,

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:13.060
beating the previously dominant graph neural
networks and transformers on eight of twelve

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.440
targets under the first data split and nine of
twelve under the second.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.820
On weather,

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:26.200
it outperforms the WeatherBench baseline on every
metric in the simpler two-predictor setting,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:30.580
and it even beats models that were pre-trained on
large amounts of simulated data on several temperature metrics.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.960
This is the first demonstration that spherical CNNs
are viable neural weather models.
